\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces T gates per iteration of the coherent oracle over those of the cheapest compile-time synthesis (cube, Reed--Muller, or affine cover), for threshold tests $\mathcal  {M}=\{y:y<\tau \}$, against the number $k$ of marked canonical inputs. All 20 instances per family, $n=4$ to 14, and $\tau \le 2^{n-1}/4$: 400, 400, and 540 cases. Below the dashed line the coherent oracle needs fewer T gates. Logarithmic axes; coinciding points overlap.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:threshold}{{2}{9}{T gates per iteration of the coherent oracle over those of the cheapest compile-time synthesis (cube, Reed--Muller, or affine cover), for threshold tests $\mathcal {M}=\{y:y<\tau \}$, against the number $k$ of marked canonical inputs. All \val {thr.seeds} instances per family, $n=4$ to 14, and $\tau \le 2^{n-1}/4$: \val {thr.N.cases}, \val {thr.L.cases}, and \val {thr.R.cases} cases. Below the dashed line the coherent oracle needs fewer T gates. Logarithmic axes; coinciding points overlap}{figure.2}{}}
